# The aeb release aeo is developed and released against.
#
# One bare version string (last non-comment line). Read it the way the
# Aether/aeb tooling reads AETHER_PIN:
#
#     grep -v '^#' AEB_PIN | tr -d '[:space:]'
#
# WHAT THIS IS — and how it differs from AETHER_PIN. AETHER_PIN is a HARD
# floor: below it `ae build` cannot even compile aeo's sources (std.spec, the
# skip verbs, the run_summary fix). AEB_PIN is SOFTER on purpose, because
# aeb is a SEAM, not a compiler aeo links against:
#
#   * BUILD-TIME. aeo's binary can be emitted by `aeb` (per LLM.md's repo
#     topology: "built BY aeb (or `ae build`)"). Plain `ae build` also works
#     — the release path and the everyday `sh test/run-spec.sh` path both go
#     through `ae`, not `aeb` — so aeb is not on the critical build path the
#     way `ae` is. When you DO drive the build through aeb, this is the
#     release it was validated with.
#   * RUN-TIME. Mid-composition aeo may shell out to build an artifact:
#     `run_capture("aeb", ["app:image"], env)` (LLM.md, "The seam to aeb").
#     This is DEMAND-DRIVEN — no aeo code path invokes aeb unconditionally,
#     so a box that never asks a composition to build an image never needs
#     aeb present at all. When a composition DOES reach for aeb, this names
#     the release whose CLI surface (`aeb <target>`, its output layout under
#     target/<module>/) aeo expects.
#
# Because the coupling is a CLI contract across a process boundary — argv in,
# artifacts on disk out — not a linked ABI, aeo tolerates a range of aeb
# versions at runtime. This pin is the KNOWN-GOOD one: the aeb aeo's docs,
# examples and seam were last checked against. Treat it as "what to install
# if you're setting up a box to exercise the aeb seam", not "aeo refuses to
# start below this".
#
# WHY a SEPARATE file rather than a line in AETHER_PIN or LLM.md. aeb and
# Aether version independently (aeb 0.297.0 rode Aether 0.645.0; the numbers
# are unrelated), and a machine-readable file lets the same one-liner above
# fetch it — the same shape aeb itself uses for AETHER_PIN/AETHER_FETCH. A
# prose mention in LLM.md would drift; a bare-number file is greppable by
# tooling and by the next person setting up the seam.
#
# WHEN TO BUMP. Move this on EVIDENCE, exactly like AETHER_PIN:
#   - aeo starts relying on an aeb CLI flag / output-layout an older aeb
#     lacks, or
#   - an aeb release fixes a seam problem aeo actually hit (a target that
#     built wrong, an output path that moved).
# Not for novelty. aeb cutting a new release is not a reason to touch this.
#
# 0.297.0 — the first recorded aeb floor for aeo. Established while pinning
# the toolchain forward (Aether 0.645.0); aeb 0.297.0 is the release the
# sibling checkout was at (../aeb == v0.297) and the one this repo's aeb
# seam is documented against. This is a BASELINE, not an evidence bump:
# before now aeo carried no aeb pin at all (aeb is a seam, and the tree has
# no unconditional aeb build/run edge), so there was nothing to build below.
# Recording it closes the "we depend on aeb but never say which aeb" gap.
0.297.0
